From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: win32u: WinSta0\Default is the user's desktop

On Windows, WinSta0\Default is the interactive user's desktop, and programs
name it explicitly: Mozilla-derived launchers and updaters put it in
STARTUPINFO.lpDesktop. In a Stained Glass session the user's desktop is a
virtual one named "shell" (HKCU\Software\Wine\Explorer\Desktop), so such a
child was put on a separate, empty "Default" desktop with no shell: its
windows could not be created ("no driver could be loaded", explorer failed
to start). LibreOffice's first start relaunches itself that way and never
showed a window; the compatibility suite found it.

A request for Default on WinSta0 now means the desktop the user's
configuration names, as it does when no desktop is given. Other stations
(services' __wineservice_winstation) and other desktop names are unchanged,
and without a configured desktop Default is still Default.

Gate: test/default-desktop-gate.sh -- a child started with lpDesktop
WinSta0\Default in a shell session lands on "shell" and creates a window.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/winstation.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/winstation.c
@@ -1062,7 +1062,18 @@
     }
     if (buffer || !NtUserGetThreadDesktop( GetCurrentThreadId() ))
     {
+        static const WCHAR defaultW[] = {'D','e','f','a','u','l','t',0};
         char buffer[4096];
+
+        /* On Windows, WinSta0\Default is the user's interactive desktop, and
+         * programs name it explicitly (Mozilla-derived launchers and updaters
+         * put it in STARTUPINFO.lpDesktop). Where the user's desktop is
+         * configured under another name (a virtual desktop: HKCU\Software\
+         * Wine\Explorer\Desktop, as Stained Glass sessions set "shell"), that
+         * is the one they mean: WinSta0\Default would be a desktop with no
+         * shell, where their windows cannot be created. */
+        if (desktop && !wcsicmp( desktop, defaultW ) && (!winstation || !wcsicmp( winstation, winsta0 )))
+            desktop = NULL;
         str.Buffer = (WCHAR *)(desktop ? desktop : get_default_desktop( buffer, sizeof(buffer) ));
         str.Length = str.MaximumLength = lstrlenW( str.Buffer ) * sizeof(WCHAR);
         if (!dir) dir = get_winstations_dir_handle();
